      "note": "The halant at the end of a word - before a space, punctuation, a danda, a digit or the end of the text - is a plain virama, as Unicode text writes a word-final one (\u0905\u0930\u094D\u0925\u093E\u0924\u094D, not \u0905\u0930\u094D\u0925\u093E\u0924\u094D\u002BZWNJ; the Gujarati tables read it so too). Before a letter it stays \u094D\u002BZWNJ, the visible halant."
